      "S4"
    ],
    "word_count": 51,
    "html": "<p>Barbara Peterson Burwell is an American philanthropist and former Miss USA who became Minnesota's first national titleholder in 1976. A St. Olaf graduate and daughter of a state Supreme Court justice, she later led the Rodney and Barbara Burwell Family Foundation, supporting educational and charitable institutions alongside her husband and sons.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Barbara Peterson Burwell shared her experience of pageant competition in Becoming a Beauty Queen: The Complete Guide, written with her sister, Polly Peterson Bowles. The book offered a practical account of a world both sisters had entered, extending her involvement beyond her own time as a contestant.\n\nHer family's connection to the University of Denver grew through her three sons' education and her service on parent councils. The family foundation helped fund a career centre designed to connect students, alumni and employers. Its services include interview preparation, networking and professional clothing for students who need it, giving the family's educational support a practical purpose.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 91,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Full reference page confirms joint book; University's2019 gift account and2020 completed-centre report establish cause, donor identity and practical services."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S1",
      "S2",
      "S7"
    ],
    "word_count": 104,
    "html": "<p>Barbara Peterson Burwell shared her experience of pageant competition in Becoming a Beauty Queen: The Complete Guide, written with her sister, Polly Peterson Bowles. The book offered a practical account of a world both sisters had entered, extending her involvement beyond her own time as a contestant.</p>\r\n<p>Her family's connection to the University of Denver grew through her three sons' education and her service on parent councils. The family foundation helped fund a career centre designed to connect students, alumni and employers. Its services include interview preparation, networking and professional clothing for students who need it, giving the family's educational support a practical purpose.</p>\r\n"
  },
